# Lighthouse HTML reports — the JSON is the machine-diffable artifact we
# commit; HTML is the human view and adds ~800KB per route per run.
docs/perf/lighthouse-*.report.html

# Mobile-matrix screenshots — a full sweep is 120 PNGs / ~48MB per run.
# We commit only the curated evidence subset referenced in the matrix
# doc (force-add what we want; gitignore the rest). Regenerate the full
# sweep via `bash scripts/capture-mobile-matrix.sh` when needed.
docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/**/*.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-iphone-se__home__01-at-rest.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-iphone-se__home__02-overlay-overview.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-iphone-se__home__03-consent-storage.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-iphone-se__ecommerce-catalog__01-at-rest.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-iphone-13__home__01-at-rest.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-pixel-5__home__01-at-rest.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-pixel-5__home__02-overlay-overview.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-ipad-mini-portrait__ecommerce-product__01-at-rest.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-ipad-mini-landscape__ecommerce-cart__01-at-rest.png
!docs/perf/mobile-matrix-screenshots/2026-04-25/matrix-ipad-mini-landscape__home__01-at-rest.png

# Claude subagent memory — per-machine, not project artifact
.claude/agent-memory/
.claude/settings.local.json
scripts/claudish/denylist.txt

# guv-gitignore — appended by /guv:scaffold
# guv-core-start
# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*-service-account.json
*-credentials.json
# Claude Code: personal overrides, not committed
.claude/settings.local.json
# Auto-generated agent memory — the reviewer writes this
# on the first /eval or /handoff (/guv:-namespaced under the plugin).
# Ignored by default so it doesn't sit untracked in every consumer project.
# A team that wants shared agent memory can force-add it
# (git add -f .claude/agent-memory/) and remove this line.
.claude/agent-memory/
# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Docker sandbox (opt-in tier)
sandbox/*.log
sandbox/tmp/
# guv context-wall migration-nudge marker ([16.2]; context-management.sh surface —
# a machine-local did-fire flag so the one-time grandfather nudge fires once, not
# every session; runtime artifact, not tracked)
.claude/.context-wall-migration-nudged
# guv context-wall continue-guidance marker ([16.4]; context-management.sh surface —
# a machine-local did-fire flag so the one-shot continue-mode "author a window if you
# want an explicit compaction point" guidance fires once, not every session; runtime
# artifact, not tracked)
.claude/.context-wall-continue-guided
# guv metering runtime artifact (handoff Step 3 writes the measured suite
# runtime here; meter.sh reads it — transient, rewritten each session, not
# tracked). The committed append-only metering logs (metering.ndjson /
# calibration.ndjson) are deliberately NOT ignored — they are shared evidence.
.claude/metering/.last-suite-runtime
# guv recorded battery verdict (battery-result.sh — run-core-tests.sh records its
# verdict here so the QA stages downstream read it instead of each paying for its
# own battery run). Machine-local and tree-specific: it carries a fingerprint of
# the exact working tree it ran against, so a committed copy would be stale for
# everyone who pulled it.
.claude/metering/.last-battery-result
# guv gate log ([25.10] — gate-log.sh appends one line per review-gate invocation;
# the handoff audits this session's commits against it). Deliberately NOT ignored,
# for the same reason as the metering logs: it is shared evidence, and a coverage
# record only one machine can see attests nothing to anyone else. Named here so its
# absence from the ignore set reads as a decision rather than an oversight.
# guv-core-end
